otengine/godot/issues/comments/3968791685","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116821#issuecomment-3968791685","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116821","id":3968791685,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sjvSF","user":{"login":"DexterFstone","id":92402263,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYHyVw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92402263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone","html_url":"https://github.com/DexterFstone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T19:40:24Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T19:46:40Z","body":"> I can't quite make out the bug with just your description. Your video looks to be working correctly at a first glance as well.\n> \n> * What are you expecting to happen?\n> * What happens instead?\n> \n> Edit: Also please test issues with the latest stable release when reporting bugs.\n\nWhen changing type, the script should be normal, not gray (in normal case the script will be removed completely); it is not possible to detach the script.\n\n<img width=\"134\" height=\"67\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1d94aed4-64b1-46bc-8b30-940e34fda486\" />\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3edde7cb-4102-4043-88a4-e53c35f07a6e\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3968791685/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3971634927","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116821#issuecomment-3971634927","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116821","id":3971634927,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sulbv","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T08:54:01Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T08:54:01Z","body":"The gray script icon is a feature that attempts to mimic custom named classes as real classes. Scripts are still attached to objects, but the editor doesn't allow you to detach a script (though you can extend the script instead).\n\nIf you add a base type node and then manually attach a script, you can detach it. If you immediately add a custom type node, it is saved with the `metadata/_custom_type_script` attribute, which tells the editor to prevent detaching the script. You can remove this attribute manually in the scene file, and the script icon will return to its normal behavior. Alternatively, you can use the \"Change Type...\" option in the context menu.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3971634927/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]